  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict and Political Economy Analysis Fund (CAPAF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CAPAF will enable British Embassy Juba (BEJ) to commission bespoke analysis to inform and shape the design and delivery of other SSPP components as well as broader UK policy and programming in South Sudan. The CAPAF will enable BEJ to quickly source research and analysis by relevant experts to fill knowledge gaps in &#x2018;live&#x2019; conflict and stability policy thinking. These will include stand-alone analytical products (e.g. papers, slides decks), more regular analysis (e.g. monthly or quarterly conflict mapping), and either one-off conflict sensitivity services from or core funding to established conflict sensitivity service providers such as the CSRF (e.g. conflict sensitivity audits and conflict sensitivity training).</narrative>
  </description>
